{"kind":"request","text":"G3 second head: durable application-owned presence (plan 033 order step 6; decision 72c9d5e5 point 3; grow note notes/2026-10-17-grow-operation-application-design.md, section 6.1 presence and open question 3; members-and-presence note on planner/member-presence-20261018, section 5, for the fact ref). Needs the first G3 head, landed at main 426504d8. Start now, before G5a or beside it at your choice, and before G5. A separate request, promise and review from the first head's.\n\nScope. Presence as state on the site scope, in the existing declared item form, no new native form, no signer index, no history scan, no device location.\n- One presence item per member, created by a bounded admin provisioning act under `grow.configure` with a duplicate-member guard, in an initial `unknown` state: provisioning never records physical presence or absence.\n- `arrive` and `leave` remain the only presence-reporting acts and transition the signer's own item under a signer-member guard: arrive moves A to B; leave checks the current room and refuses a wrong-room leave by name, so arrive(A), arrive(B), leave(A) keeps the member in B.\n- The item carries the room ref, the state (`unknown`, `present`, `away`) and a fact ref to the last reporting entry (arrive or leave), so a reader can name the entry that recorded the current state.\n- The carousel's for rule reads this item through the existing declared root-site read; a member with no item, or an item in `unknown`, is unavailable, never absent; the first head's last-100 window logic is dropped.\n- Choose the exact item and act steps within the existing form and record the provisioning and bounds decisions in the implementation note.\n\nDone when, in the kit's test host with the kit's checks, each named in the review request with its witness: (a) provisioning creates the item in `unknown` and refuses a duplicate by name; (b) arrive(A), arrive(B), leave(A) leaves the member present in B with the fact ref naming the leave's refusal-free predecessor, and the wrong-room leave is refused by name; (c) the tender's task routing of the first head holds on the item for present, away and unknown members, with unknown unavailable; (d) the same selections hold after more than one hundred site entries, which the first head's window could not prove; (e) app-only data, quiet context, receipts, stale refusals, resize. Gate passed once at the head; measurements labelled by how they were taken; checker approval at the exact head. One head.\n\nOut of scope: the mixed what-needs-me queue (a later head), a device's own location, the journey's attention loop, G5a and G5.","body":{"conditions":"presence is a per-member site-scope item provisioned in unknown state and transitioned only by arrive and leave, carrying a fact ref to its last reporting entry; the first head's routing holds on it beyond the last-100 window; gate passed once; checker approval at the exact head","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}